-- title:
--   Support transfer at level N for J₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N,q,p$ be natural numbers with $N\neq 0$, $q\neq 0$, $q$ and $p$ prime and $q\nmid N$, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$, and let $\mathfrak m$ be a maximal ideal of the abstract Hecke algebra [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlg`](def/HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura.html#L14) $=\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell:\ell\text{ prime}]$ containing the image of $p$ and satisfying [`FreyPackage.IdealGoodPrimeCurveCongruence p (N*q) W 𝔪`](def/FreyPackage_MazurAttachmentApparatus.html#L29): for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid \Delta_W$, $\ell\nmid Nq$ and $\ell\neq p$, the element $X_\ell - a_\ell(W)$ lies in $\mathfrak m$, where $a_\ell(W)$ is the trace of Frobenius of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$. Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll.html#L8), i.e. for every prime $\ell$ the integrality, finiteness, principal-divisor, fundamental-identity and norm-formula data defining the Hecke correspondence at level $N$ and $\ell$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ are available, and [`ModularCurve.HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L25), i.e. the resulting endomorphisms $T_\ell$ of $J_0(N):=$ the degree-zero divisor class group [`ModularCurve.JZero N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115) of the level-$N$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ commute pairwise. Let finally $S$ be a finite set of primes, each dividing $Nq$. Then, for the `HeckeAlg`-module structure on $J_0(N)$ obtained by evaluating polynomials at these commuting operators, [`ModularCurve.SupportTransfer N W p S 𝔪 (ModularCurve.JZero N)`](def/ModularCurve_SupportTransfer.html#L44) holds: if the predicate `HasLowerLevelTorsion S 𝔪 (ModularCurve.JZero N)` holds, then the ideal `exitIdeal N W p` is not the unit ideal.
--
--   This is the support-comparison step in Ribet-style level lowering: $\mathfrak m$-torsion in $J_0(N)$ which is annihilated away from the primes of $S$ forces the ideal of the level-$N$ Hecke algebra generated by $p$ and the differences $T_\ell-a_\ell(W)$ to be proper, so that it is contained in a maximal ideal. It is used by [`ModularCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_of_hasLowerLevelTorsion_of_isGoodPrimeFor`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_of_hasLowerLevelTorsion_of_isGoodPrimeFor) and by [`WeierstrassCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_div_of_cast_eq_one_of_isUnramifiedAt_sqf`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_div_of_cast_eq_one_of_isUnramifiedAt_sqf) to produce a mod $p$ eigenform of level $N$ whose residual representation agrees with that of $W$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_supportTransfer_jZero.lean

